// @check
// @error `as i32` propagates null — use `as!` to trap instead, or `as?` to take the null here; to propagate it, annotate the enclosing function's return type
// A bare `as` over a type parameter pinned at no number can miss, as it can at a fractional
// `f64`, so it owes the same propagation home (D2791).
function k<T>(u: T) { u as i32 }
print(k<string>("s"))
